# Chat and attachments

Follow the **latest user message**. Ask vs Agent is per send, not the
whole thread — a prior "currently in Ask mode" assistant note is stale
once the composer is Agent ("I switched to Agent" / yes after that copy
is write). Stamp THIS SEND as a prefix on the latest user ModelMessage
and in `composerModeTurnRule` — never as a mid-thread `role: "system"`
message (Gemini: system messages only at the beginning). Agent mode may edit when they asked to
write; empty sections and ready attachments are not a request to draft.
Greetings ("hi", "hello", "thanks") must not search or call write tools
(Document `draft_field` / Analytics `write_column`). Classifier:
`classifyChatUserIntent` in `src/lib/ai/chat/user-intent.ts` (rules) plus
`resolveChatUserIntent` in `src/lib/ai/chat/resolve-user-intent.ts`
(Flash-Lite when rules would emit `ambiguous_agent_mode` or
`ambiguous_polite_request` such as "can you do the same for X", and on
Document chat when the text looks like a worksheet dump). The same call may set
`switchToAnalytics` when Lite is ≥0.75 sure the destination is the Analytics
grid — Report chat then shows a Switch to Analytics button; clicking it
sets Analytics and resends the original request. A yes / go for it after
that copy is a write. Stub chat,
timeout, and parse failures keep the rules decision with no widget.
Retrieval maps those turns to focused (`reason: no_task`) and skips
kickoff evidence. A yes after the assistant offered to draft is a write
request. Agent-mode "go for it" / "do it" is write even when the prior
turn dumped findings instead of matching the offer regex. Polite leftovers
(`can you` without a produce verb, "do the same") go to Lite — they are
not `question_or_lookup`. Real lookups (`what` / `who` / `do you`) stay
on rules. Missing-work complaints ("nothing was filled", "why isn't the
table filled", "I don't see the change", "suggestions are not landing",
"refusing to make an edit", "only summarising") are write on Agent
(`reason: missing_work`) so Lite is skipped. An explicit "insert the
suggestion" / "edit the document" turn reads the section first, then the
next step must call `draft_field` (`replaceFilledField: true`) when they
asked to redraft / replace / make 15.N as a different equipment ID (or
"insert it" after that rewrite was dumped in chat), `draft_rtm_table`
when a QSR RTM table is in `@` scope, `propose_edit` for leftover 15.N
heading / 15.N.1 / 15.N.3 / 15.N.5 prose ("go for 15.N.1", "make these",
"insert suggestions for 15.N.1" — create the cards if none are open;
quote heading + following paragraph only, never Table N / GFM — the
server strips those and still lands the paragraph; after two `edit_table`
fails on that turn, recover with `propose_edit` instead of emptying
tools). "Add a table to 15.N.x" under a heading already in the saved box
is `edit_table` `create_table` with `afterAnchor` — not leftover-prose
`propose_edit` (do not strip the table and rewrite the paragraph). Preview
marks the inserted table, not the last table in the box (15.N.8 extraneous).
Then `edit_table` for any other table, or `propose_edit`. A filled
CVP equipment identity rewrite is a whole-field `draft_field`, not
cell-by-cell `edit_table`. Leftover prose after those tables landed is
`propose_edit`. Do not claim Agent mode is read-only or
paste a markdown table. ELR section numbers
in chat are the Contents outline (3.10 Monitoring, 3.12 Preventive
Maintenance, 3.15 Access Control). A printed Table N is only the number on
the context map. Agent read keeps write tools
registered on the ToolSet; `advertisedTools` hides them. A remapped
`unsupported_tool` for a write tool unlocks them on the next step
(Document `prepareReportChatStep` and Analytics `prepareAnalyticsChatStep`).
`list_suggestions` lists open / approved / dismissed AI cards (section + preview, no comment ids). Wrap-up
must not claim a fill unless a tool this turn returned proposed, drafted,
or applied. Persist rewrites wrap-up that claimed a table or fill when no
write tool returned those statuses (`rewriteUnlandedWriteParts`). CVP
equipment `read_section` snapshots the same bound/normalized clone that
writes stale-check, so compact (`10000 L` → `10k L`) or collapsed
duplicate headings cannot bounce every `edit_table` as `section_changed`.

Search attachments **before** `ask_user`, `draft_field`, or a `<placeholder>`
for report facts (batch, date, result, equipment ID, requirement ID, design
output, verification objective, ECO/DCR). Exception: when intent is **write**
and the target section is **filled or partial**, call `read_section` first
(gate on fill state + write intent — not draft/fill verbs). Review against
criteria and any cached AI Check gap hints; if there are no material gaps
and they did not already name a change, report that it is already drafted
and ask whether they want a specific change. A named cell or document edit
is that change: after the read, call `edit_table` or `propose_edit`. Explicit
rewrite language is the escape hatch. If there are gaps,
make a targeted edit. Do not pad length or invent gaps. If a gap conflicts
with an omit-if rule, ask once whether to include it. Do not quiz
them for facts already in the section or that you would put in `hint`.
An unset title-page identity field with two mutually exclusive answers in
the attachments (ELR: both Vial and Cartridge, `formatScope` unset) is a
fork: `ask_user` once before drafting. That is not a fact already in
retrieved evidence. Type-owned `chat.contextIdentity` surfaces those fields
and `chat.identityFields` lists the scalars Agent fills with `draft_identity`
(one suggestion card for the whole header — Apply / Dismiss; remaining-section
treats a complete proposal as done; duplicate document numbers fail at
propose and at Apply; no citations — those fields print on the cover and
running header). QSR
Capacity / Size (`keepUnits`) restores the printed unit from this turn's
cited quotes when the model writes a bare number (`8000` → `8000 L`);
conflicting units stay bare, and 8000 is not converted to 8 KL.
`prepareStep` hides `draft_field` while that gate is active. The document
index (filename/topics) is not evidence. Evidence preview is already in the
system prompt when kickoff retrieval hits.

After a cited search hit, a locate/read (`read_document_page` /
`document_outline` / Analytics scan-extract), or two empty greps, hide
`search_documents` for the rest of the turn (`searchLoopDirective` shared
with Analytics). An identifier-only grep that hits a protocol family
keeps search open until every attached protocol family (DQ, IQ, OQ, PQ) has been queried (any order) (`shouldKeepRtmProtocolSearchOpen`) — a hit on one family is
not enough while DQ / IQ / OQ / PQ are still unsearched. Document-chat attachment cover sheets (ATTACHMENT NO. /
certificate-of locators, `divider=true`), split tables (`continues=true`,
Page N of M with N < M), and title lists without identifier values
(`identityIncomplete=true` — SOP Name / Document Name without a document
number) are not a complete cited data page: they
set `keepSearchOpen` and `searchHitCount` treats `dividerHits` /
`identityIncompleteHits >= returnedCount` as 0 so the following page can
be read or grep can continue. `read_document_page`
includes the next page as `continuation` when the transcript prints Page N
of M. Analytics still hides after a real cited page (it does not keep grep
open for split tables). Do not hide search while a document review is
`in_progress` / `ready_to_finish`, or when a tool result sets
`keepSearchOpen` / `status: unsupported_facts`. Prior-turn tool JSON is compacted before
`convertToModelMessages` (page transcripts, finish findings, write
payloads). Finished document-review coverage is rehydrated across turns
when the ready-attachment coverage key is unchanged (the key is the
selected documents' **full** page counts plus the current section/objective,
not a silent 300-page prefix); comprehensive retrieval does not force another walk on a zero
coverage delta unless the latest message is explicit pushback
(`you missed`, `look again`, `re-check`, a test-family code). Pushback
skips rehydrate so a finished session does not hide
`start_document_review`. `planReviewPages` queues pages that score on the current
objective (floor 8; nearby same-file pages if almost nothing matches). ELR
inventory tables score against the live column schema (headers / aliases, plus
a typed `{modifier} {section noun}` that is not URS language such as
`monitoring systems`), nested method names (non-viable / settle plate / glove /
LAF). Preferred-filename boost is PRQR/PRQP (monitoring no longer prefers
the alarm-trend PDF). Preferred files with
zero hits are still queued as a stratified sample (PRQR/PMC on breakdowns,
CCF/CAPA/PRQR on QMS, cap `REVIEW_PREFERRED_MISSING_PAGE_CAP`) so a few CSV-IQ
/ FAT headers cannot floor-8-pad them out — not every page of a 200-page CCF.
CSV-OQ / CSV-IQ / RTM / URS pages
score 0 unless they look like a dated result table (QSR RTM and
Operating Range skip URS demotion and prefer `urs` / `user requirement`
filenames plus the URS heading family; 5.1–5.6 share one `|obj:qsr_rtm`
finish so a URS walk unlocks the sibling tables — including Gemini NL
objectives such as control philosophy / GMP requirements). Header-only UNCONTROLLED
COPY / Sign/Date chrome is 0. Haystack uses outline + pageContext + the first
4000 transcript characters. `start_document_review`
for an ELR inventory still omits a single-file pin so PRQR / PRQP / PQR
rows can split, but it does not page-list a file typed as a different
inventory (a calibration planner is not QMS). Monitoring and Breakdowns drop
alarm-trend files and cite the already-drafted Alarm Trends table instead. Running-header `document no`
is not a column hit. A truncated matching finish that cannot unlock
`edit_table` (floor-8 skip of PRQR) does not `forceStart` again — remaining
section must not mill until the 270s abort. The planning chip names queued files. Complementary grep ORs
those column phrases. `REVIEW_PAGE_FETCH_CAP`
(2500) is listing safety only. ELR inventory walks then cap at
`REVIEW_INVENTORY_WALK_CAP` (48) so one continue can drain scored CCF
pages; DV catalogs keep the listing cap. QSR Table 3
(`qsr_qualification_documents`) is not ELR qualification history: do not
demote URS or walk 48 protocol body pages — queue the first two pages of
every attached lifecycle file and omit `attachmentIds`. Collapse `|obj:`
onto that cover walk only when every named identity shares the cover
plan — mixed SOP Number / Reference Number copy is a scored body walk.
QSR RTM / Operating Range omit `attachmentIds` so the server keeps the URS
(a 12-page URS is a 12-page walk), not DQ/IQ/OQ/PQ bodies.
`continue_document_review` stops starting batches after ~60s and round-robins
batches across attachments. `start_document_review`
reports `truncated` / `skippedDocuments`. Call `list_attachments` first
when the file set is unknown. Rehydrate only a finish with `status=complete`
and `truncated !== true`.

`edit_table` `insert_rows` prefers `afterRowKey` (first-cell text) over
`afterRow`. Sequential `insert_rows` on the same table fold into the open
card (`mergeInsertRowsOperations` / `foldSameTableRowOperations`) — a
first-row `edit_cells` of the seeded blank row folds with later inserts
the same way. The first pending row is not in the saved table, so a later
`afterRowKey` of that first-cell would otherwise `bad_scope`. Same-turn
same-table `insert_rows` and scaffold `edit_cells` are serialized;
`edit_cells` of a filled row and ops on other tables stay parallel.
`edit_cells` prefers `rowKey` (first-cell text, e.g. URS-13)
over `row`. Each `edit_cells` cell rematches by its own `rowKey` — do not
group a batch by a reused dummy numeric row. An already-filled or missing
`rowKey` sibling is dropped so remaining cells still preview. Do not insert `{ banner }` group rows; existing template banners
keep their colspan and data rows do not inherit it.
Hard facts in `draft_field` / `propose_edit` / `edit_table` are gated
against the citation ledger's served quotes (`groundDraftText`). That
gate is fact-level (`citation-exemption.ts`): never skip a whole
section. Exempt title-page / user-confirmed identity, the ELR
1 April–31 March window, and facts already written in this report
(sibling table or another section). A product this-turn `calculate`
returned is computed evidence (operands still need a page), same as a
saved analysis. Copied attachment facts still need
a page in Purpose, Responsibilities, assessments, and recaps. Tables
stay strict. Finish seeds `reviewedEvidence` (every walked page, not the
60-finding sample) so those transcripts can hydrate. Empty ledger or
pages with no quotes fail open, except QSR RTM / Operating Range / Qual
Docs / References, which fail closed when the URS or source protocol is
attached but unread. Those rows also require the fact in the same URS-N
quote window (`qsr-row-grounding.ts`) or on the URS cover / outside any
URS-N window (capacity, MOC) — a neighbour URS on the same page still
bounces. A column-major URS page (one or more blocks of IDs, then the requirement
sentences) keeps each block's sentences out of the last ID's window and
still lets every ID in that block use them, even when another row's
parameter shares a word such as glass or thickness. URS-1 does not match
URS-13. OCR-split `URS- 33` / `URS-\n33` is URS-33 before windowing.
Lettered subparts (`URS-34 a` → `URS-34a`) stay distinct windows — same
numeric stem does not continue a column-major ID run; URS-34 / 34a / 34b
belong in 5.2 (Instrument Requirement). Gold:
`glr-1301-urs-page-9.transcript.txt`.
Digits in URS-N are not a measured number. A decimal such as 25.0 is
not a measured zero. OCR-split `3 . 5` is evidence for `3.5`, not a reason
to persist `<number>` or ask the engineer to type it. Integer `3` is not
`3.5`. Integer `1600` matches OCR `1600.0` / `1600.00`, not `1600.5`.
Do not glue a numbered-list index onto the next measurement (`1. 2.5`
is not `1.2.5`). A protocol section number (`9.3.4`, `7.2`, `8.2.4`)
persists only when a retrieved page prints it. Repair search pins to
cited files when the draft named them. A named date column (Effective Date) matches the source value
next to that same label first; if the exact label is missing, the
closest date label on the page. A signature or observation date is not
that field when a closer status label exists. An explicit insert, or a
fact the engineer stated this turn, still cites a page but is not dropped.
Prior assistant chat is not a keep-source. Ask (plan) replies drop
`[filename, p. N]` on persist when that page was not retrieved this turn
or the served quote does not contain the nearby hard fact, and replace
unsourced hard facts with placeholders (attachment facts need a retrieved
quote; report/worksheet facts need `read_section` / `read_worksheet` this
turn; engineer-stated facts stay). A leading minus is part of the number
(`−15 °C` is not `15 °C`; OCR-split `- 15` is evidence for `-15`). A
leading tilde is approximate (`~50±10 RPM` is not `−50 ± 10 RPM`). A ±
window is not independent evidence for the setpoint (`50±10 RPM` is not
`−50 ± 10 RPM`). The high end of a range is not evidence for the low end
(`20 °C` is not `−20 °C to 150 °C`). Stock Complies / bare Section 13 still need a named-stage protocol page that
  either names that URS ID or topic-matches that row's Parameters in the
  protocol body (not the running header). Verified on the result line counts
  as a pass; Verified By in a signature block does not. An executed
  verification record (Actual observation / Verified By columns plus a
  signature date that is not the Effective Date / Issued On header date)
  is a pass with no pass word; an unexecuted template (no signature date)
  is not, and a fail / does-not-meet statement vetoes every pass. Unsupported family-column /
  Remarks cells clear
instead of blocking the URS copy. Persist rewrites family cells to
`{section} – {audit line}` from the protocol body page that prints
that heading, drops cover/contents `Section 8` / `13.2` cites, and
attaches an audit line to leftover number-only `12.1` only when that
same section number is on the ledger (keep `8.1` / `12.1` if pick is
null; do not swap onto a neighbour `12.4`). Family workers
reject number-only and off-topic submits so one grep cannot finish
the column.
PQ/OQ/IQ family-column numbers are
dotted (`8.2.3`, `8.1.1`, `13.6`); a printed page counter (`16`, `14`,
`Page 21 of 51`) or a logged measurement (`12.72 °C`) is cleared, and `[file, p. N]` cites the page that
prints that heading. An explicit empty `edit_cells` of filled
DQ / IQ / OQ / PQ / Remarks stays a clear (suggestion card), including when
the URS is attached but unread this turn. Protocol N/A becomes Remarks NA
only at row level (labeled Result / Remarks N/A, `not applicable for this
…`, or a bare N/A inside that URS-N window) — a stray `Model Number NA`
spec cell does not. When a saved cell differs from the request, the
`edit_table` `proposed` result carries `adjustedCells` (`requested` /
`saved`) plus `proposedRowKeys` / `proposedCellCount` / `droppedRowKeys`
so the wrap-up names only the rows on the card (one `edit_table` is one
card, not one card per URS row). The card title counts only cells that
actually change — identity Remarks and dummy leftover cells are dropped
before persist. QSR RTM family columns / Remarks on the card are the
grounded cells from chat (`edit_table` insertText) — there is no family
ranker that rewrites IQ to PQ or swaps a neighbour heading. Existing
Table 5–10 rows stored Stage + Section: open / export / chat merge keeps
URS identity and Remarks, drops Stage / Section, and leaves DQ/IQ/OQ/PQ
blank so the assistant can refill (no SQL). A page
counter (`16`) or logged reading (`12.72 °C`) in Section still clears.
Wrap-up quotes `adjustedCells.saved`
Section, not a different test heading. Every pack uses `unsupportedFactPolicy: block`
(no persist; `unsupported_facts`). On a blocked write, those tools run
one closed-set repair search (C1 retriever) pinned to cited files when
the draft named them, seed new quotes, and
re-ground the original text — not a Flash-Lite subagent. Prose leftover
`<date>` / `<identifier>` / `<number>` persist after that lookup when
the facts are still missing. Table leftovers bounce once
(`unsupported_facts` + `keepSearchOpen`) so a subsequent grep can still
fill the cell; a retry in the same turn may persist leftover `<date>` /
`<identifier>` / `<number>`, but other leftover `<…>` cells are dropped
instead of persisting `<remarks>` / `<result>`. Uncited
numbers do not `citation_move` onto a coincidental ledger page. A cited
number does not move onto another page of the same file just because the
digits appear there (PFR-1301 5 L HAS is not a rinse volume). A drafted
unit must not conflict with a different page unit (`5 L` is not
`5-10 L/m²`); a page that prints the number with no unit still supports
it. Unsupported citations next to the number are stripped. CVP considered
volume / rinse sample quantity may persist uncited as a GMP operational
floor. Analytics
`write_column` stays ungated.

## Spectrum

Document and Agent share `ChatPanel` + `StatisticalWorkspace`. Document
`/chat` and Analytics `/analytics/chat` are counterparts (section `@` plus
saved-plot `@` vs sheet/plot `@`). Composer Report | Analytics
(`chat-work-product-target`) is the same dropdown in both chromes — do not
retarget from the focused canvas pane. Mixed-thread history tags each
message Report or Analytics (`metadata.chatTarget`, stamped by the route
that handled the POST — not the client body). Legacy rows fall back to
`promptVersion` / exclusive tools; fully unknown history stays untagged.
A composer, mention, or tool change that only lands on one
chrome or one surface is incomplete. Walk UI → request body → route parser →
prompt → tools → `PLAN_MODE_CHAT_TOOL_NAMES` → retrieval-policy /
already-drafted / stub → tests → docs. Removing a control means deleting
that plumbing (`body.sectionScope`, `parseChat*`, switch-section tools,
mismatch banners) — not hiding the dropdown. Scope is `@` mentions
(`sectionScopeFromMentions`, analytics mention block). Bare `@` opens
Attachments first (nested folders of ready files), then Document sections
or Data sheets. Do not recap that list at 8. Bump
`CHAT_PROMPT_VERSION` / `ANALYTICS_CHAT_PROMPT_VERSION` when prompt copy
changes. Empty-state Document chips are `chat.examplePrompts` on the
document type (not DMAIC-hardcoded); Analytics chips stay in
`ANALYTICS_EXAMPLE_PROMPTS`. Voice dictation is the shared composer mic
(Document | Agent, Report | Analytics). Click start / click stop; no VAD.
Recording chrome is a larger level wave + “Transcript appears when you stop”
+ language chevron + white stop square.
MJ: `en-IN` / `hi-IN` / `mr-IN` in native script (Devanagari preferred). Demo/Convergent: `en-US`.
Do not translate STT to English — `LANGUAGE_RULES` keep assistant output
in English. PCM is buffered while recording; after stop, each PCM POST is one
Vertex **Gemini** transcribe (Flash-Lite, same WIF/resolver as chat). Do not call Cloud Speech-to-Text / Chirp —
the runtime SA 403s `PERMISSION_DENIED` without `roles/speech.client`.
No sticky session / SSE. Stub: `ALLOW_TEST_STUB_SPEECH`.
Monthly voice minutes are a separate Limits cap (`voice-budget`, default
100,000 minutes) in addition to the Gemini token budget; usage is
`voice_transcribe` in the AI feature table.

## Prompt / tools

- Untrusted metadata (`filename`, `description`, `documentSummary`,
  `pageContext`) → `sanitizePromptMetadata` in chat/tools. Never import that
  helper from `src/lib/attachments/`.
- New tools: register in `buildChatTools` **and** add to the Plan allowlist in
  `src/lib/ai/chat/document-review.ts` (`PLAN_MODE_CHAT_TOOL_NAMES`).
  Include `list_suggestions` (open / approved / dismissed AI cards).
  Missing from the allowlist = silent Plan-mode gap. Analytics tools stay
  off that list. File-set questions (how many attachments, which files in which
  folder, PDF vs Word, status, filename/topic) use `list_attachments`
  (`src/lib/attachments/list-catalog.ts`). Copy it into
  `ANALYTICS_DOCUMENT_TOOL_NAMES`. Do not hide it in `searchLoopDirective`.
  Arithmetic that is not printed on a page uses `calculate` (Document and
  Analytics; Plan-allowlisted; copy into `ANALYTICS_DOCUMENT_TOOL_NAMES` and
  Analytics `READ_AFTER_SEARCH_TOOLS`). This-turn products are computed
  evidence — operands still need a retrieved quote. Do not multiply in the
  model's head.
  Do not stuff an authoritative count into the Documents index instead.
  Content-inside-PDF “which files mention X” stays `search_documents`.
- A tool-input schema violation must never end the engineer's turn.
  `repairChatToolCall` clamps `InvalidToolInputError` input to the tool's own
  JSON Schema (`clampToolInputToSchema`: maxItems, maxLength, min/max, enum,
  single value → array) and retries once. Malformed JSON is still not
  rewritten. Prefer widening a bound over tightening one — the clamp is a net,
  not a licence to add tight caps. A `NoSuchToolError` for a name that is not
  loaded this turn (e.g. `edit_table` after write tools were stripped for a
  question or document-review step) remaps onto the internal `unsupported_tool`
  fallback so the stream continues with a hint — do not let `AI_NoSuchToolError`
  fail the chat. Keep that fallback out of `activeTools` / the Plan allowlist.
  On Agent read, a write-tool `unsupported_tool` unlocks the registered write
  tools on the next step (do not paste a markdown table as a stand-in).
- Analytics never asks which page to read. `ask_user` is hidden on a lookup,
  after Skip / “find it”, and after any grep (including TOC-only) until a
  page is read/scanned. Page-number questions are rejected if they still
  fire. TOC-only greps do not close search. A Skip on that form is a locate
  request (search/scan), not a placeholder. A dump with some blank cells
  must not hide `write_column` — remaining requested columns fill this turn.
- `insert_image` source=analytics copies a saved plot only when the named
  series matches (or they did not name one). If they asked for a plot that
  is not listed, return the available titles once this turn (`available_plots`)
  and say they can create additional ones in Analytics — that status is not a
  proposal (do not claim a suggestion exists). Do not insert a different
  figure, and do not call `insert_image` again to re-list. Destination wording
  ("Measure", "Deviations" / "devaition"), fillers ("the assays thing"), and
  confirmation ("yes, that one", "yes please do") are not plot names.
  Parallel `insert_image` calls in one turn serialize onto one card. Inserted
  plots copy the saved Analytics preview at the same 600px display width
  as right-click Insert graph (`CHART_DISPLAY_WIDTH_PX`). Do not shrink by
  a 300px height cap — that turns a sixpack into a thin unreadable strip.
- `insert_image` source=document copies a cited figure from a ready PDF/DOCX
  (`filename` + `page`, optional `figure` = visualInterpretation Figure N).
  PDFs rasterize that page; Word copies an embedded PNG/JPEG (header/letterhead
  skipped). Word drawings that are not rasters cannot be copied — attach a
  PDF of the same file. CSV/XLSX ingest as markdown pages + `document_tables`
  (no figures); `insert_image` stays PDF/DOCX only. Search first; do not invent
  a figure. `available_figures`
  is not a proposal. Stay off the Plan allowlist.
- Document **and** Agent chrome **propose** (red/green `ai_fix` comments;
  nothing lands until Apply / Dismiss, including Apply all / Dismiss all
  for one or more open suggestions). Same-turn `propose_edit` calls
  serialize; locatable spans within 20 characters on the same field fold
  into one card (no per-field budget). Lead-in / table / figure /
  citation-split / cell-scope edits stay separate. Plan-mode allowlist
  does not gain edit tools. There is no `commit` edit-policy path.
- Kickoff retrieval (`buildAutoEvidence`) is fail-soft (timeout / no creds →
  `""`). Do not block the turn on embeddings.
- Report and Analytics `stopWhen` is Cancel or the wall-clock deadline
  (`CHAT_SERVER_ABORT_MS` from request start, not from `streamText`).
  Do not add a tool-step cap — users must never hit one. Do not persist
  a “ran out of steps / ask me to continue” notice. Multi-section Agent
  drafts persist a `pending_plan` on the chat session. After each turn
  the client POSTs `Continue the remaining sections.` with `autoContinue`
  (auto-continue user rows stay hidden; one live remaining-section widget
  sits **below** the transcript while the queue is running, above Working…
  / Resume — collapsed `N completed · M remaining` (or `M remaining` when
  none are done yet), expand for done / running / pending. After Cancel or
  a new typed prompt pauses the queue, the widget sits **above** that later
  prompt, not under the whole thread). Do not persist
  or show “The assistant stopped before finishing” when that next POST
  will run. Three remaining-section turns on the same in-progress item
  without completing it (`CHAT_PLAN_SAME_SECTION_TURN_LIMIT`, including
  review-only 270s aborts) pause the queue (`same_section_limit`); Resume
  clears attempts. The remaining-section chip
  spins only while the turn is running; it shows Paused on Cancel and hides
  when every remaining section is drafted. MJ ELR evidence sections stay
  in progress after `edit_table` until the same turn drafts the assessment
